  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, UNICEF enhanced the health environment by securing MoPH agreements on user fees and collaborating on community health strategies. UNICEF launched the HAYAT Newborn program, focusing on policy, service access, quality, and care continuity, particularly post-discharge follow-up, a national referral system, and a newborn mortality audit system. Community outreach by PHCs is an important new effort that promotes better policies and SOPs while improving overall health system delivery. Efforts in mental health included a new sub-strategy. UNICEF also initiated a digital transformation roadmap for optimizing the health system and championed increased community-level surveillance and response to prevent humanitarian disasters.;</narrative>
   </title>
